I apologize.

733
00:38:43,880 --> 00:38:45,600
My heart goes out to you.

734
00:38:45,600 --> 00:38:46,740
I know what that feels like.

735
00:38:46,740 --> 00:38:49,060
Jesus knows what that feels like.

736
00:38:49,060 --> 00:38:51,100
And I'd love to pray with you after service

737
00:38:51,100 --> 00:38:52,940
if you're so called to that.

738
00:38:52,940 --> 00:38:54,620
But Paul says,

739
00:38:54,620 --> 00:38:57,840
we need not grieve like the rest who have no hope.

740
00:38:57,840 --> 00:39:00,680
There's an important distinction here.

741
00:39:00,680 --> 00:39:05,120
And I've heard this talked about from the pulpit,

742
00:39:05,340 --> 00:39:06,800
and you won't hear it from me

743
00:39:06,800 --> 00:39:08,040
unless the Lord calls me to repentance.

744
00:39:08,040 --> 00:39:11,140
But it's the phrase, don't grieve.

745
00:39:11,140 --> 00:39:13,580
But that's the temptation though, right?

746
00:39:13,580 --> 00:39:15,740
Paul doesn't say don't grieve.

747
00:39:15,740 --> 00:39:17,820
And I've heard, I'm sure, well-intentioned pastors say,

748
00:39:17,820 --> 00:39:19,440
don't cry for them, they're rejoicing with Jesus.

749
00:39:19,440 --> 00:39:22,220
In an attempt to help someone through their loss

750
00:39:22,220 --> 00:39:23,480
or a way to comfort someone.

751
00:39:23,480 --> 00:39:26,520
But I'm gonna stand by this statement again

752
00:39:26,520 --> 00:39:27,940
unless Jesus calls me repentance.

753
00:39:27,940 --> 00:39:29,020
Grieve.

754
00:39:29,020 --> 00:39:31,320
Grieve the loss of a loved one,

755
00:39:31,320 --> 00:39:32,960
a grandparent, a child, a friend.

756
00:39:32,960 --> 00:39:34,420
Grieve that loss.

757
00:39:34,760 --> 00:39:35,180
It's okay.

758
00:39:35,180 --> 00:39:38,640
You're not somehow less of a Christian if you grieve.

759
00:39:38,640 --> 00:39:41,380
And I believe God grieves with us.

760
00:39:41,380 --> 00:39:45,040
Back to John 11 where Martha testifies to the resurrection

761
00:39:45,040 --> 00:39:46,140
in verse 35,

762
00:39:46,140 --> 00:39:48,940
Jesus weeps over his friend Lazarus.

763
00:39:48,940 --> 00:39:51,940
Not because Jesus didn't have faith.

764
00:39:51,940 --> 00:39:54,740
Not because Jesus didn't have hope in the resurrection.

765
00:39:54,740 --> 00:39:56,380
He is the resurrection.

766
00:39:56,380 --> 00:40:00,680
So I believe Jesus weeps with us when tragedy strikes.

767
00:40:00,680 --> 00:40:03,220
Jesus weeps with us when we lose a loved one

768
00:40:03,220 --> 00:40:05,660
because as creator, as God,

769
00:40:05,660 --> 00:40:07,580
he mourns with us because his creation

770
00:40:07,580 --> 00:40:09,760
was never supposed to experience this kind of hurt.

771
00:40:09,760 --> 00:40:13,900
So the world has language around death that's final.

772
00:40:13,900 --> 00:40:17,460
Phrases like died, passing away, no longer with us.

773
00:40:17,460 --> 00:40:19,920
There's finality to that language.

774
00:40:19,920 --> 00:40:20,380
An end.

775
00:40:20,380 --> 00:40:23,140
A missing piece.

776
00:40:23,340 --> 00:40:25,940
There's finality to a world without the hope of Jesus.

777
00:40:25,940 --> 00:40:29,920
The ultimate Christian hope continues.

778
00:40:29,920 --> 00:40:33,660
And it uses language that does not give death the power it does not deserve.

779
00:40:33,660 --> 00:40:36,960
Death is an enemy of God, according to Paul.

780
00:40:37,620 --> 00:40:41,380
And it does not deserve power, respect, or authority.

781
00:40:41,380 --> 00:40:44,800
So Jesus told his listeners in Luke 8, 52,

782
00:40:44,800 --> 00:40:46,300
the child's not dead.

783
00:40:46,300 --> 00:40:47,700
She's only sleeping.

784
00:40:47,700 --> 00:40:53,280
Well, Jesus, I mean, Jesus was mocked by the onlookers when he said this

785
00:40:53,280 --> 00:40:54,900
because, like, let's face it, right?

786
00:40:54,900 --> 00:40:56,680
Death is not that difficult to understand.

787
00:40:56,680 --> 00:40:59,540
And they're like, this Jewish rabbi doesn't know what death is.

788
00:41:00,560 --> 00:41:03,960
But I think Jesus, see, Jesus uses this unique term,

789
00:41:03,960 --> 00:41:06,740
and Paul adopts it, this idea of sleep.

790
00:41:06,740 --> 00:41:09,560
What I think Jesus and the later apostle Paul are doing

791
00:41:09,560 --> 00:41:13,360
is not giving death the power or respect it does not deserve.

792
00:41:13,360 --> 00:41:15,440
Now, let's unpack this a little bit.

793
00:41:15,440 --> 00:41:17,940
What happens eventually after you sleep?

794
00:41:17,940 --> 00:41:20,680
You wake up.

795
00:41:20,680 --> 00:41:22,460
You are on it.

796
00:41:22,460 --> 00:41:26,740
Let's look back at 1 Corinthians 15, starting in verse 50.

797
00:41:26,740 --> 00:41:30,540
What I'm saying, brothers and sisters, is this.

798
00:41:30,560 --> 00:41:33,420
Flesh and blood cannot inherit the kingdom of God,

799
00:41:33,420 --> 00:41:36,220
nor can corruption inherit incorruption.

800
00:41:36,220 --> 00:41:39,540
Listen, I am telling you a mystery.

801
00:41:39,540 --> 00:41:42,840
We will not all fall asleep, but we will all be changed in a moment

802
00:41:42,840 --> 00:41:44,560
in the twinkling of an eye at the last trumpet.

803
00:41:44,560 --> 00:41:48,320
For the trumpet will sound, and the dead will be raised incorruptible,

804
00:41:48,320 --> 00:41:49,320
and we will be changed.

805
00:41:49,320 --> 00:41:53,200
For this corruptible body must be clothed with incorruptibility,

806
00:41:53,200 --> 00:41:56,540
and this mortal body must be clothed with immortality.

807
00:41:56,540 --> 00:41:59,760
When this corruptible body is clothed with incorruptibility,

808
00:41:59,760 --> 00:42:02,780
and this mortal body is clothed with immortality,

809
00:42:02,780 --> 00:42:06,800
then the saying that is written will take place.

810
00:42:06,800 --> 00:42:09,960
Death has been swallowed up in victory.

811
00:42:09,960 --> 00:42:14,800
Where death is your victory, where grave is your sting.

812
00:42:14,800 --> 00:42:17,580
Folks, don't hear self-righteousness from me.

813
00:42:17,580 --> 00:42:19,520
I don't have all the answers to life's questions.

814
00:42:19,520 --> 00:42:23,360
What I do have is hope, and that's what I want for you guys too,

815
00:42:23,360 --> 00:42:25,120
and that's the reason for my message.

816
00:42:25,680 --> 00:42:29,200
This apprenticeship under King Jesus isn't about being the best moral person in the room,

817
00:42:29,200 --> 00:42:30,640
or a holier-than-thou person.

818
00:42:30,640 --> 00:42:33,640
If you're thinking that, you've missed the gospel.

819
00:42:33,640 --> 00:42:37,420
And I'd love to, this is the gospel, that Jesus is Lord.

820
00:42:37,420 --> 00:42:41,380
Let me tell you this, that Jesus Christ didn't come to make bad people good.

821
00:42:41,920 --> 00:42:43,740
He came to make dead people alive.

822
00:42:43,740 --> 00:42:47,460
See, humanity in the fall of the garden is slipping into oblivion,

823
00:42:47,460 --> 00:42:52,440
and Jesus came that he might reclaim us as his beloved creation back into life.

824
00:42:52,940 --> 00:42:59,080
Both the abundant life now, having this hope in Jesus' promises and these things not seen,

825
00:42:59,080 --> 00:43:02,740
and an eternal life later where we bask in his new creation and new bodies,

826
00:43:02,740 --> 00:43:06,200
where we can experience God to the fullest extent imaginable.

827
00:43:06,200 --> 00:43:09,900
We have never experienced someone too far gone for Jesus.

828
00:43:09,900 --> 00:43:12,980
He, as the most loving father we could ever know,

829
00:43:12,980 --> 00:43:15,080
throws a celebration when we return to him.

830
00:43:15,080 --> 00:43:18,120
He desires his creation to commune with him.

831
00:43:18,640 --> 00:43:22,180
And this death that we've been experiencing as a people,

832
00:43:22,180 --> 00:43:24,000
this is a byproduct of our rebellion.

833
00:43:24,000 --> 00:43:26,520
His desire is that we all come back,

834
00:43:26,520 --> 00:43:29,400
not to a father who's condescending and is ready to berate us at the door,

835
00:43:29,400 --> 00:43:33,920
but one who with tear-filled eyes welcomes us home and weeps with us

836
00:43:33,920 --> 00:43:36,540
as we experience the hurt that sin has caused his creation.

837
00:43:36,540 --> 00:43:40,660
And he's asked us to partner with him to wipe it from the face of the earth.

838
00:43:40,660 --> 00:43:43,940
Revelation 21, 3-5 says,

839
00:43:43,940 --> 00:43:47,400
Look, God's dwelling place is with humanity.

840
00:43:48,640 --> 00:43:51,140
And he will live with them and they will be his people,

841
00:43:51,140 --> 00:43:54,200
and God himself will be with them and be their God.

842
00:43:54,200 --> 00:43:57,060
He will wipe every tear from their eye.

843
00:43:57,060 --> 00:43:59,480
Death will no longer exist.

844
00:43:59,480 --> 00:44:02,280
Grief, crying, pain will no longer exist

845
00:44:02,280 --> 00:44:03,940
because the previous things have passed away.

846
00:44:03,940 --> 00:44:05,560
There's that language around finality, right?

847
00:44:05,560 --> 00:44:08,860
Grief, crying, and pain are passing away.

848
00:44:08,860 --> 00:44:12,360
So then the one seated on the throne said,

849
00:44:12,360 --> 00:44:14,480
Look, I am making everything new.

850
00:44:15,480 --> 00:44:19,060
I came across this poem during my ordination studies,

851
00:44:19,060 --> 00:44:20,520
and it's something that impacted me,

852
00:44:20,520 --> 00:44:22,720
and I'd like to share it with you guys today.

853
00:44:22,720 --> 00:44:28,860
It's like 19th century German, so bear with me.

854
00:44:28,860 --> 00:44:29,320
Not German.

855
00:44:29,320 --> 00:44:32,680
I can't read to it in German, but it's kind of the old English.

856
00:44:33,620 --> 00:44:35,920
T'was by thy darts I am slain.

857
00:44:35,920 --> 00:44:38,280
Or death, thou hast conquered me.

858
00:44:38,280 --> 00:44:40,800
T'was by thy darts I am slain.

859
00:44:40,800 --> 00:44:46,160
But Christ shall conquer thee, and I shall rise again.

860
00:44:46,160 --> 00:44:49,280
Time hastens on the hour.

861
00:44:49,280 --> 00:44:51,860
The just shall rise and sing.

862
00:44:52,700 --> 00:44:54,180
O grave, where is your power?

863
00:44:54,180 --> 00:44:55,900
O death, where is your sting?

864
00:44:55,900 --> 00:44:59,260
See, resurrection is the Christian hope.

865
00:44:59,260 --> 00:45:02,280
Jesus was the first fruits of that resurrection,

866
00:45:02,280 --> 00:45:03,980
and he promises us the same.

867
00:45:03,980 --> 00:45:07,380
John 6, 39 through 40 says,

868
00:45:07,380 --> 00:45:09,700
This is the will of him who sent me,

869
00:45:09,700 --> 00:45:12,540
that I should lose none of those that he has given me,

870
00:45:12,540 --> 00:45:14,840
but should raise them up on the last day.

871
00:45:15,740 --> 00:45:18,560
For this is the will of my Father,

872
00:45:18,560 --> 00:45:21,060
that everyone who sees the Son and believes in him

873
00:45:21,060 --> 00:45:22,360
will have eternal life,

874
00:45:22,360 --> 00:45:24,320
and I will raise him up on the last day.

875
00:45:24,320 --> 00:45:27,600
If you're questioning this,

876
00:45:27,600 --> 00:45:32,060
won't you humble yourself before the Creator and King today?

877
00:45:32,060 --> 00:45:35,920
Are you tired of doing life on your own?

878
00:45:35,920 --> 00:45:38,660
Tired of lacking hope of what's to come?

879
00:45:38,660 --> 00:45:41,520
Let me reassure you with something.

880
00:45:41,520 --> 00:45:43,880
You were never meant to do this alone.

881
00:45:45,200 --> 00:45:45,920
Jesus is here,

882
00:45:45,920 --> 00:45:50,560
and I confidently claim that Jesus is Lord of everything.

883
00:45:50,560 --> 00:45:53,660
The resurrection proved that Jesus is reliable

884
00:45:53,660 --> 00:45:55,120
in the things he said and his promises.

885
00:45:55,120 --> 00:45:59,000
He's the Father who loves his children more than you can imagine.

886
00:45:59,000 --> 00:46:02,140
Revelation 3, 20 echoes this point.

887
00:46:02,140 --> 00:46:03,520
I stand at the door and knock.

888
00:46:03,520 --> 00:46:05,920
If anyone hears my voice and opens the door,

889
00:46:05,920 --> 00:46:09,680
I will come into him and eat with him and he with me.

890
00:46:09,680 --> 00:46:13,380
Are we tired of not having hope for tomorrow?

891
00:46:14,580 --> 00:46:16,080
Jesus, he is our hope.

892
00:46:16,080 --> 00:46:21,260
I got a quote from John Piper that I thought encapsulated the worldview idea.

893
00:46:21,260 --> 00:46:22,720
It says,

894
00:46:22,720 --> 00:46:32,300
few people seem to realize that the resurrection of Jesus is the cornerstone to a worldview that provides the perspective to all of life.

895
00:46:33,580 --> 00:46:35,160
Now, the two questions that we started with.

896
00:46:35,160 --> 00:46:39,300
Hopefully, you have some interpretative tools to help you answer these.

897
00:46:39,300 --> 00:46:42,100
What is the ultimate Christian hope?

898
00:46:42,100 --> 00:46:43,280
How would you answer this?

899
00:46:43,280 --> 00:46:51,280
And two, what hope is there for change, rescue, transformation, and new possibilities within the world of the present?

900
00:46:52,320 --> 00:46:54,060
I'm going to answer these from my perspective.

901
00:46:54,060 --> 00:46:56,940
But you guys can probably guess them from my sermon.

902
00:46:56,940 --> 00:47:00,000
The ultimate Christian hope for me is the resurrection.

903
00:47:00,000 --> 00:47:06,840
Both in Jesus' resurrection and future promised resurrection, where we live glorified with God in new heavens, new earth.

904
00:47:07,560 --> 00:47:18,720
Even when I feel like my world is crumbling and around me, viewing and interpreting my realities through the lens of the resurrection helps me cope and I think helps me better understand the heart of God for his creation.

905
00:47:20,220 --> 00:47:26,320
And question two, what hope is there for change, rescue, and transformation, and new possibilities within the world of the present?

906
00:47:26,320 --> 00:47:31,060
And I'll quote somebody that has far more clout than me in this.

907
00:47:31,060 --> 00:47:34,300
St. Augustine does a fabulous job of answering it.

908
00:47:34,300 --> 00:47:39,380
The joyful news that he is risen does not change the contemporary world.

909
00:47:39,380 --> 00:47:43,660
Still before us lies work, discipline, and sacrifice.

910
00:47:44,600 --> 00:47:52,680
But the fact of the resurrection gives us the spiritual power to do the work, accept the discipline, and make the sacrifice.

911
00:47:52,680 --> 00:47:57,400
So this week, I'd like to end, I'd like to close with communion.

912
00:47:57,400 --> 00:48:02,900
And hopefully you grabbed a cup, the miracle meal, on your way in.

913
00:48:02,900 --> 00:48:05,660
If not, I'll give you a couple seconds to grab one.

914
00:48:05,660 --> 00:48:12,260
These are easier to open.

915
00:48:13,600 --> 00:48:15,260
Maybe, I might have spoke too soon.

916
00:48:15,260 --> 00:48:28,800
As you guys find your way to the communion table, I'd like to talk a little bit about this today.

917
00:48:28,800 --> 00:48:37,120
In the same way the travelers on the road to Emmaus didn't see Jesus until he blessed the bread and broke it,

918
00:48:37,120 --> 00:48:39,280
we practice open communion.

919
00:48:39,840 --> 00:48:46,420
If you have not recognized the risen Savior, today is a great day to do that.

920
00:48:46,420 --> 00:48:52,700
May Christ show himself to you in the broken bread as we bless it.

921
00:48:52,700 --> 00:48:57,320
This bread represents his body broken for you.

922
00:48:57,320 --> 00:49:03,880
He is more than a political, he is the king of more than a political or ideological kingdom.

923
00:49:04,340 --> 00:49:06,580
He is king of all creation, the whole world.

924
00:49:06,580 --> 00:49:11,980
If you have submitted your life to the risen Savior, I encourage you to examine your life and worldview.

925
00:49:11,980 --> 00:49:15,940
Are we viewing this world as resurrection promised people?

926
00:49:15,940 --> 00:49:21,620
Will we have no fear of the world around us because our king has been raised victorious over death?

927
00:49:22,740 --> 00:49:28,240
If you have communion and so choose, let's open those together and partake of the bread together.

928
00:49:28,240 --> 00:49:31,220
Christ's body broken for us.

929
00:49:40,020 --> 00:49:43,080
In the same way, Christ's blood was spilt for us.

930
00:49:43,080 --> 00:49:47,460
So we drink the juice, remembering his sacrifice, but celebrating the promises that lie ahead.

931
00:49:47,460 --> 00:49:49,280
Christ's blood spilt for you.

932
00:49:56,340 --> 00:50:01,480
I'd like to close this week with a benediction from the apostle Peter, found in 1 Peter 1, 3-9.

933
00:50:01,480 --> 00:50:07,040
Blessed be the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ.

934
00:50:07,040 --> 00:50:13,660
Because of his great mercy, he has given us new birth into a living hope through the resurrection of Jesus Christ from the dead

935
00:50:13,660 --> 00:50:18,760
and into an inheritance that is imperishable, undefiled, and unfading.

936
00:50:18,760 --> 00:50:21,540
Kept in heaven for you.

937
00:50:22,340 --> 00:50:27,700
You are being guarded by God's power through faith for a salvation that is ready to be revealed in the last time.

938
00:50:27,700 --> 00:50:34,020
You rejoice in this, even though for a short time, if necessary, you suffer grief in various trials

939
00:50:34,020 --> 00:50:41,580
so that the proven character of your faith, more valuable than gold, which though perishable, is refined by fire,

940
00:50:41,580 --> 00:50:47,380
may result in praise, glory, and honor at the revelation of Jesus Christ.

941
00:50:47,380 --> 00:50:48,480
Amen.

942
00:50:48,480 --> 00:50:51,080
Go in peace, church.

943
00:50:52,340 --> 00:51:20,020
Can I take a picture of that phrase?

944
00:51:20,020 --> 00:51:21,820
Because I was writing it down, and you changed it.

945
00:51:21,820 --> 00:51:23,040
I need to take a picture of that phrase.

946
00:51:23,040 --> 00:51:23,820
Can you see some of the real eyes?

947
00:51:23,820 --> 00:51:24,700
Oh, yeah.

948
00:51:24,700 --> 00:51:25,400
John Piper's?

949
00:51:25,400 --> 00:51:26,620
Also, I wrote this one down.
